  "summary": "An economizer recovers heat from boiler flue gas to preheat the feedwater before it enters the drum. Banks of (often finned) serpentine tubes sit in the gas duct after the main heating surfaces. Gas flows down while water flows up — counter-flow — so the gas leaves cooler and boiler efficiency rises.",
